\### Patients

Inclusion criteria

1. Age between 12 and 60 years at the time of surgery;
2. Male and female patients;
3. History of unilateral anterior cruciate ligament (ACL) injury;
4. Patients who underwent single-bundle "Over-The-Top" ACL reconstruction with lateral extra-articular tenodesis and any associated procedures;
5. Patients who received medical clearance to return to sport at least 12 months prior to the assessment;
6. Patients who provided informed consent to participate in the study.

Exclusion criteria

1. Patients who are no longer reachable;
2. Patients who decline consent to participate in the study;
3. Cardiopulmonary diseases;
4. History of severe musculoskeletal injuries resulting in absence from sports activities for more than 28 days, unrelated to the index injury;
5. Inability to perform the motor tests required by the study protocol;
6. Discontinuation of sports activities after surgery.

   * Healthy Population

Inclusion criteria

1. Age between 12 and 60 years;
2. Male and female subjects;
3. Subjects who have not undergone ACL reconstruction and have no history of relevant injuries or musculoskeletal conditions that could affect the performance of the motor tests or the planned kinematic assessments;
4. Tegner Activity Scale score ≥5;
5. Subjects who provided informed consent to participate in the study.

Exclusion criteria

1. Subjects who decline consent to participate in the study;
2. Cardiopulmonary diseases;
3. Inability to perform the motor tests required by the study protocol.
